# Branding needs NO configuration — both variables below are overrides. Out of the box the webapp
# mirrors the backend's archives into `.branding-cache` and reads, in order:
#   .branding-cache               the sync cache (always first: it mirrors the backend, which owns the
#                                 list of brands). Written and owned by server-middleware/branding-sync.js.
#   ../deployment/configurations  your brand sources, as a fallback before the first sync lands.
# Build them with `node packages/branding/scripts/build-dev-brandings.ts`; the active brand is switched
# live in the admin Branding tab, or pinned for dev with OCELOT_ACTIVE_BRANDING. Iterate on a single
# brand without a rebuild:
#   node packages/branding/scripts/build-brand-archive.ts <brand-dir> --watch
# then edit brand.config.ts — the backend serves the rebuilt archive at once and the webapp picks it up
# within OCELOT_BRANDING_SYNC_TTL_MS (60s; set it to 0 to see every change on the next refresh).
#
# OCELOT_BRANDING_ASSETS_DIR REPLACES the read locations above (`:`-separated, an earlier root shadows
# a later one per brand id — nothing is ever deleted to settle that). The cache stays first regardless.
# OCELOT_BRANDING_CACHE_DIR moves the cache; point it at a directory NOTHING else writes — never at
# deployment/configurations, or the sync would compete with your own brand builds.
# OCELOT_BRANDING_ASSETS_DIR=
# OCELOT_BRANDING_CACHE_DIR=
# OCELOT_BRANDING_SYNC_TTL_MS=
# OCELOT_ACTIVE_BRANDING=
